Java 11 Features — Interview Focus ⭐

Java 11 is an LTS (Long-Term Support) version and came after Java 8. For interviews, remember these major features:

1. var in Lambda Parameters ⭐⭐⭐

Java 10 introduced var for local variables. Java 11 extended it to lambda parameters.

(var a, var b) -> a + b

You can also use annotations:

(var a, @NotNull var b) -> a + b

Important: You cannot mix var and normal types:

(var a, b) -> a + b;       // ❌
(var a, int b) -> a + b;   // ❌
2. New String Methods ⭐⭐⭐

Java 11 added several useful methods.

isBlank()
String s = "   ";

System.out.println(s.isBlank());  // true

Difference:

"".isEmpty();      // true
"   ".isEmpty();   // false

"".isBlank();      // true
"   ".isBlank();   // true
lines()
String str = "Java\nSpring\nReact";

str.lines()
   .forEach(System.out::println);

Output:

Java
Spring
React
strip()
String str = "  Java  ";

System.out.println(str.strip());

strip() is Unicode-aware, unlike the older trim().

stripLeading()
"  Java".stripLeading();

Result:

Java
stripTrailing()
"Java  ".stripTrailing();

Result:

Java
repeat()
System.out.println("Java ".repeat(3));

Output:

Java Java Java
3. HttpClient API ⭐⭐⭐

Java 11 introduced a new HTTP Client API.

Before:

HttpURLConnection

Java 11:

HttpClient
HttpRequest
HttpResponse

Example:

HttpClient client = HttpClient.newHttpClient();

HttpRequest request = HttpRequest.newBuilder()
        .uri(URI.create("https://example.com"))
        .GET()
        .build();

HttpResponse<String> response =
        client.send(request, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofString());

System.out.println(response.body());

It supports:

HTTP/1.1
HTTP/2
synchronous requests
asynchronous requests
4. Files.readString() and Files.writeString() ⭐⭐

Java 11 made reading/writing text files easier.

String data = Files.readString(Path.of("test.txt"));

Writing:

Files.writeString(
    Path.of("test.txt"),
    "Hello Java 11"
);
5. Single-File Source-Code Execution ⭐⭐

You can run a Java source file directly:

java HelloWorld.java

Instead of manually doing:

javac HelloWorld.java
java HelloWorld

Useful for small programs/scripts.

6. Epsilon Garbage Collector

Java 11 introduced the Epsilon GC, a garbage collector that performs no garbage collection.

It is mainly useful for:

performance testing
memory allocation testing
short-lived applications

It's not normally used for production applications.

7. ZGC — Experimental

Java 11 introduced Z Garbage Collector (ZGC) as an experimental low-latency garbage collector.

The goal was to handle very large heaps while keeping GC pause times extremely low.

8. Flight Recorder

Java Flight Recorder (JFR) became available in OpenJDK 11.

It is used for:

JVM monitoring
performance analysis
troubleshooting
identifying CPU/memory problems
🔥 Java 8 vs Java 11 — Interview Question
Java 8	Java 11
Lambda	var in lambda parameters
Stream API	New String methods
Optional	HttpClient
Method Reference	Files.readString()
Default methods	Files.writeString()
java.time	Single-file execution
CompletableFuture	ZGC
Functional interfaces	Epsilon GC
	Flight Recorder
🧠 Easy trick

Remember Java 11 as:

String + HTTP + Files + var + GC

Java 11
   ↓
String methods
   ↓
HttpClient
   ↓
Files read/write String
   ↓
var in Lambda
   ↓
ZGC / Epsilon
   ↓
Flight Recorder

Most important for your interviews: String.isBlank(), strip(), lines(), repeat(), var in lambda, HttpClient, and single-file execution.